# #733 — this file exists to UN-ignore, and that is the whole point.
#
# The repository root .gitignore carries `*.js` (line ~1104) and `**/[Bb]in/*` (line ~94), both
# aimed at build output elsewhere. In an AdonisJS app they match the application's own SOURCE:
# ace.js is the entrypoint every npm script invokes, and bin/ holds the server and console
# bootstraps. So when this sample was added, git dropped exactly the three files that make it
# runnable, and the sample shipped with `dev`, `start` and `build` all pointing at nothing.
#
# Negation works here because the root patterns exclude FILES within bin/ rather than the
# directory itself — a directory excluded outright cannot be re-included by a later rule.
!ace.js
!bin/
!bin/*.ts

# Real build output, which should stay ignored.
build/
